#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34ea56b4-2066-5aaf-aea9-08515803fc0b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating an Expression With Parentheses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9eec8bb-467d-59e7-b5cd-40dc6828473c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9eec8bb-467d-59e7-b5cd-40dc6828473c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478163} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a89af28-e9aa-5c06-8dee-00cb06e2dec2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "372b47e2-6ed6-5dd6-9cf6-680592eef643" :question/math-academy-id "q-134035" :question/problem "Margaret and Ivana each bought $3$ blackberry muffins and $5$ strawberry muffins. In total, they bought$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$muffins." :question/worked-solution "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total number of muffins.\n\nSince each of them bought $3$ blackberry muffins and $5$ strawberry muffins, the number of muffins each of them bought is:\n\n$$\n{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{blackberry muffins}}+{{5}_{⏟}}_{\\text{strawberry muffins}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person bought this number of muffins, and there are $2$ people, we must multiply the number of muffins by $2.$ Therefore, the total number of muffins is:\n\n$$\n{{(3+5)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+5)\\times 2 & =(3+5)\\times 2 \\\\  & =8\\times 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n8\\times 2=16\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85f7df01-47df-5ca6-bdc2-9485017b51bd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Two-Digit Number by a Two-Digit Number: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b53b2738-8572-5261-b027-3991a5619e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "336" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53b2738-8572-5261-b027-3991a5619e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "336" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478091} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f1060b-99a4-54a9-9d90-4de8db023ee4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdb9c372-6491-56bd-a5e0-6ea4e60521c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134036" :question/problem "At the sale, there are $14$ tables. If there are $24$ muffins on each table, then there are{{field-1}}\nmuffins in total." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total number of muffins, we need to multiply $14$ by $24.$\n\nSo, we write it this way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  &  &  & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the ones:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\times 4=56\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the tens:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}14\\times 20=280\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}56+280=336\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $14\\times 24=336.$\n\nTherefore, there are $336$ muffins in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a1e476-39d5-529d-8632-c5dce93b8ed7" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing When the Hundreds Digit Is Less Than the Divisor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e19410f8-5141-5879-b4e1-7cc2e9dbb964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19410f8-5141-5879-b4e1-7cc2e9dbb964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478180} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3934810-291e-50dd-a02f-1abe03f05b32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad2f9bd5-68e3-5ec1-9893-522d4b4c3aca" :question/math-academy-id "q-134037" :question/problem "If $8$ people made all the muffins for the sale, and each made the same number of muffins, then each person made{{field-1}}\nmuffins." :question/worked-solution "We know that there are $336$ muffins in total. So, each person made $336÷8$ muffins.\n\nWe start by writing down the question using long division notation:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that $3$ (the number of hundreds in $336$) is less than the divisor $8.$ Therefore, we should consider both the hundreds and tens:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$↓$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $33÷8=4\\,\\text{R}\\,1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over tens: $4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $8\\times 4=32$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $33-32=1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Bring down: $6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNext, we consider the ones:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}3\\,\\phantom{|}6}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\boxed{\\text{0}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $16÷8=2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over ones: $2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $8\\times 2=16$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $16-16=0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe get the remainder $0$, so the division is done.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n336÷8=42.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b7bb96c-c682-54da-98d7-aa1b6960ee9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Sum of an Improper Fraction and a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8cb4cda-24d2-5289-9fdc-ed366390b2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8cb4cda-24d2-5289-9fdc-ed366390b2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478097} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e540d7b-743f-5bd7-a258-f559a1a1adde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff575d67-9751-56f2-8a79-bde7f1b08899" :question/math-academy-id "q-134038" :question/problem "Mark bought $3$ liters of strawberry juice and $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice. How much juice did Mark buy in total? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\nMark bought$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of juice." :question/worked-solution "To find out how much juice Mark bought in total, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n3+\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nTo add $3$ and $\\frac{7}{4},$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $4.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen we put this fraction over a denominator of $4$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 4}{1\\times 4}=\\frac{12}{4}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{4}+\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{4}+\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{12+7}{4}=\\frac{19}{4}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n19÷4=4\\,\\text{R}\\,3=4\\,\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mark bought $4\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ liters of juice in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ee87e73-843c-5596-b1f2-341d4e7266f8" :knowledge-point/title "Converting the Final Answer to a Mixed Number: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "130239fb-94ea-5f7b-b527-6609027ac4c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "130239fb-94ea-5f7b-b527-6609027ac4c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477769} :answer-field/id #uuid "b18b7f1a-9848-5ccf-aabe-0086594b08a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "568d8931-746a-5ddb-bec0-b2b44679e4f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-134039" :question/problem "Of the $3$ liters of strawberry juice Mark bought, he gave $\\frac{2}{5}$ liters to his niece Rose. As a mixed number, Mark has$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$liters of strawberry juice left." :question/worked-solution "To find out how much strawberry juice Mark has left, we must calculate the difference $3-\\frac{2}{5}.$\n\nTo subtract $\\frac{2}{5}$ from $3,$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $5.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $5$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{15}{5}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{15-2}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n13÷5=2\\,\\text{R}\\,3=2\\,\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mark has $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ liters of strawberry juice left."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198431 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf381e5b-c6ba-5255-8d6a-797576f71baf" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing Fractions When the Least Common Denominator Equals the Product of Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a9145b-e89f-5644-b84a-b9289034dc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30a9145b-e89f-5644-b84a-b9289034dc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477824} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e189e91-c3f4-5f41-b25e-59687be1e346" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e19cccb1-4d45-55c6-bcb1-2380acb7eef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19cccb1-4d45-55c6-bcb1-2380acb7eef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478181} :answer-field/id #uuid "835d0de7-324f-5219-bfef-fa0e01e7ec74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edc909fc-f87e-5b26-96f1-797620d48727" :question/math-academy-id "q-134040" :question/problem "After Rose takes her share of strawberry juice, Mark's remaining amount of strawberry juice is{{field-1}}\nthan the remaining amount of orange juice because $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$\n{{field-2}} $\\frac{7}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "Mark has $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ liters of strawberry juice and $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice remaining.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $5\\times 4=20.$\n\nTo put $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}=\\frac{13\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{52}{20}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{7}{4}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{7\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{52}{20}$ and $\\frac{35}{20}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $52>35,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{52}{20}>\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n> \"After Rose takes her part of strawberry juice, Mark's remaining amount of strawberry juice is $>$ than the remaining amount of orange juice because $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}>\\frac{7}{4}.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "476cf433-d982-5f14-89be-48aea2abaf55" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db74ecda-0569-54ba-ac08-7d66a1a014b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db74ecda-0569-54ba-ac08-7d66a1a014b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478166} :answer-field/id #uuid "905a5d8b-fc52-5fb2-af2a-3605fabca6ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17030b91-3cba-5c59-ac6a-c1eb417052bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-134041" :question/problem "Mark drank $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the amount of orange juice that he bought. What **exact** amount of juice did Mark drink?\n\n*Remember that Mark bought $\\frac{7}{4}$ liters of orange juice.*\n\nMark drank\n{{field-1}}\nliters of orange juice." :question/worked-solution "We know that Mark has $\\frac{7}{4}$ of a liter of orange juice.\n\nTo find the fraction of a liter that Mark drank, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{2}$ by $\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 7}{2\\times 4}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mike drank $\\frac{7}{8}$ liters of orange juice."}]}
